@* Plan A02 (pass 28b): a broken unit's rout in the RtPh. The page gives the obligations already written for the view and the units that may still
   rout (ruling R23.1); the planner decides the route, the Interdictions, and the Failure to Rout. A03 RoutObligations stays inline here: it is one list. *@
<ActionSection Title="Rout" Key="rout">
<RuleHelp Id="rout-help" Summary="Broken units that must rout, or are under DM, rout one at a time, the ATTACKER's first, toward the nearest woods or building; Low Crawl moves one Location and is never Interdicted. One that ends the RtPh ADJACENT to a Known unbroken armed enemy unit, or stays in the Open Ground hex it had to leave, is eliminated or surrenders (A10.5, A10.52, A20.21).">
    In the RtPh the ATTACKER's broken units rout first, one at a time, then the DEFENDER's (A10.5). A broken unit must rout when a Known unbroken
    armed enemy unit is ADJACENT or in its Location, or it is in Open Ground in the LOS and Normal Range of a Known enemy unit; it may rout under DM.
    It has six MF (a wounded SMC three) and must reach the nearest woods or building Location it can this RtPh, never moving closer to a Known armed
    enemy unit that has seen it, nor ADJACENT to one. Entering Open Ground in the LOS of an unbroken enemy unit is Interdicted by a NMC; Low Crawl
    is one Location using all its MF and is never Interdicted (A10.52, A10.53). As the RtPh ends a broken unit ADJACENT to its enemy, or one that did
    not rout from the open, is eliminated, or surrenders to an ADJACENT Good Order enemy (A20.21).
</RuleHelp>
@* Pass 70 (ruling R70.11): at the start of the RtPh, before any unit routs, the side's units a Known enemy unit allows to break voluntarily, by hex,
   leaders first; the planner decides which (A10.41). *@
@if (BreakRows.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="toolbar" id="voluntary-break">
        <UnitSelectionList Rows="@BreakRows" Selected="@BreakSelected" CssClass="voluntary-break-unit" Legend="Voluntary Break" OnToggle="@OnBreakToggle" />
        <button id="propose-voluntary-break" disabled="@(BreakSelected.Count == 0 || Busy)"
                title="@(Busy ? "A proposal is being made; wait for it." : BreakSelected.Count == 0 ? "Tick the units that break first."
                    : "Before any unit routs, a unit in the LOS and Normal Range of a Known armed unbroken enemy unit, or ADJACENT to one, may break so as to rout this RtPh; it is under DM, and a leader's break calls for a LLTC (A10.41, A10.62, A10.2).")"
                @onclick="@(() => OnProposeBreak.InvokeAsync())">Propose: Voluntary Break</button>
    </div>
}
@if (RoutsOffered)
{
@* The user, 2026-10-21: the broken units by hex, each hex first offered the routes open to all its units, each unit's own routes behind a
   checkbox; every unit named after its hex. Each rout is still its own, one at a time (A10.5). *@
    var hexGroups = UnitGrouping.Groups(Obligations, item => item.Unit, PlaceOfUnit);
<ul id="rout-obligations">
    @foreach (var group in hexGroups)
    {
        var routing = group.Items.Where(item => Units.Any(unit => unit.Id == item.Unit)).ToArray();
        var shared = Shared(routing);
        <li class="rout-hex" data-hex="@group.Hex">
            @if (group.Hex is { } hex)
            {
                <strong>@hex</strong>
            }
            <ul>
                @foreach (var item in group.Items)
                {
                    <li @key="item.Unit" class="rout-obligation" data-unit="@item.Unit">
                        @Prefix(item.Unit)@DisplayText.Sentence(Say(item.Text))
                        @* Pass 65 (ruling R65.11; D6.1): a broken Passenger names no route; it routs beneath its vehicle with all its MF. *@
                        @if (item.Beneath is { } vehicle)
                        {
                            <button type="button" class="rout-beneath" data-unit="@item.Unit" data-vehicle="@vehicle" disabled="@Busy"
                                    title="It spends all its MF and is placed on foot beneath the vehicle, in its Location (D6.1, D5.311)."
                                    @onclick="@(() => OnBeneath.InvokeAsync(item.Unit))">Rout @At(item.Unit) beneath @Say(vehicle)</button>
                        }
                        @* Pass 31d (design D3): a way to each place the rout may end, each on a line of its own (the table player); the button fills
                           the route, which stays the player's to change. *@
                        @if (EachUnit && item.Routes is { Count: > 0 } ways)
                        {
                            <ul class="rout-ways">
                                @foreach (var way in ways)
                                {
                                    <li><button type="button" class="link use-route" data-unit="@item.Unit" data-route="@way.Route" title="Chooses this unit and fills its route; you may still change it."
                                                @onclick="@(() => OnUseRoute.InvokeAsync((item.Unit, way.Route)))">@Prefix(item.Unit)@Say(item.Unit): use the route to @Say(way.Target)</button></li>
                                }
                            </ul>
                        }
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>
            @if (shared.Count > 0)
            {
                <div class="toolbar rout-group-ways">
                    @foreach (var way in shared)
                    {
                        <button type="button" class="rout-group" data-hex="@group.Hex" data-route="@way.Route" disabled="@Busy"
                                title="Each unit routs in turn along this route, with its own Interdiction (A10.5); the first one refused stops the rest."
                                @onclick="@(() => OnRoutGroup.InvokeAsync(([.. routing.Select(item => item.Unit)], way.Route)))">
                            @(routing.Length == 1 ? $"Rout {Prefix(routing[0].Unit)}{Say(routing[0].Unit)} to {Say(way.Target)}" : $"Rout the {routing.Length} units in {group.Hex} to {Say(way.Target)}")
                        </button>
                    }
                </div>
            }
            else if (routing.Length > 1 && routing.All(item => item.Routes is { Count: > 0 }))
            {
                <p class="toolbar-note">No route is open to all of them: tick "each unit's own routes" below.</p>
            }
        </li>
    }
</ul>
@if (Obligations.Any(item => item.Routes is { Count: > 0 }))
{
    <label class="rout-each"><input type="checkbox" id="rout-each" checked="@EachUnit" @onchange="@(args => EachUnit = args.Value is true)" /> Show each unit's own routes</label>
}
<div class="action-form">
<ActionFormGroup Legend="Unit and assistance">
    <label>
        Broken unit
        <select id="rout-unit" value="@Unit" @onchange="@(args => OnUnit.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            <UnitOptions Units="@Units" Text="@At" />
        </select>
    </label>
    @* Pass 70 (ruling R70.12): an unbroken leader stacked with the unit may rout with it (A10.711); only the leaders the planner allows are offered. *@
    @if (Leaders.Count > 0)
    {
        <label title="He routs with the unit, takes no Interdiction NMC himself, adds his leadership DRM to its NMC, and is eliminated if it fails (A10.711).">
            Leader routing with it
            <select id="rout-with-leader" value="@Leader" @onchange="@(args => OnLeader.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
                <option value="">none</option>
                <UnitOptions Units="@Leaders" Text="@At" />
            </select>
        </label>
    }
    @* Pass 31d (design D2; A10.4): what a laden unit leaves and keeps, said only for a unit that carries more than its IPC. *@
    @if (Load is { Length: > 0 })
    {
        <span id="rout-load" class="toolbar-note">@DisplayText.Sentence(Say(Load))</span>
        @if (Loads.Count > 1)
        {
            <label>
                It keeps
                <select id="rout-keep" value="@Keep" @onchange="@(args => OnKeep.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
                    @foreach (var load in Loads)
                    {
                        <option value="@load.Id">@Say(load.Label)</option>
                    }
                </select>
            </label>
        }
    }
</ActionFormGroup>
<ActionFormGroup Legend="Route">
    <LocationField Id="rout-route" Label="Route (hexes in order)" Name="the rout route" Many="true" Placeholder="E6, E7" Size="24" Value="@Route" OnChange="@OnRoute" />
    <label><input id="rout-low-crawl" type="checkbox" checked="@LowCrawl" @onchange="@(args => OnLowCrawl.InvokeAsync(args.Value is true))" /> Low Crawl</label>
</ActionFormGroup>
<ActionProposalArea>
    <button id="propose-rout" disabled="@(!Units.Any(unit => unit.Id == Unit) || Route.Trim().Length == 0)" aria-describedby="propose-rout-ready" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync())">Propose: rout</button>
    @if (!Units.Any(unit => unit.Id == Unit) || Route.Trim().Length == 0)
    {
        <span id="propose-rout-ready" class="toolbar-note">Choose the unit that routs and give its route.</span>
    }
</ActionProposalArea>
</div>
}
</ActionSection>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's words for the view (pass 31c, design D11): a unit's name for its id, a Location in words.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "Say")]
    public Func<string, string>? Words { get; set; }

    private string Say(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : Words?.Invoke(text) ?? text;

    /// <summary>A unit's name with its hex, "4-6-7 squad G4 in [G4]" (the user, 2026-10-04), where no Location stands beside the name.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "SayAt")]
    public Func<string, string>? WordsAt { get; set; }

    private string At(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : WordsAt?.Invoke(text) ?? Say(text);

    /// <summary>A unit's Location, which names it and groups the broken units (the user, 2026-10-21).</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "PlaceOfUnit")]
    public Func<string, UnitPlace?>? PlaceOfUnit { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether each unit's own routes are shown; the routes open to a whole hex come first (the user, 2026-10-21).</summary>
    private bool EachUnit { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Every unit of a hex routs in turn along one route (A10.5: one at a time; the user, 2026-10-21).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<(IReadOnlyList<string> Units, string Route)> OnRoutGroup { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the page is making a rout, so a second is not asked for meanwhile.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Busy { get; set; }

    private string Prefix(string unit) => PlaceOfUnit?.Invoke(unit) is { } place ? $"{place.Where}: " : string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The routes offered to every unit of the hex that may still rout, in the first unit's order.</summary>
    private static IReadOnlyList<Way> Shared(IReadOnlyList<Obligation> routing) =>
        routing.Count == 0 || routing.Any(item => item.Routes is not { Count: > 0 }) ? []
            : [.. routing[0].Routes!.Where(way => routing.All(item => item.Routes!.Any(other => other.Route == way.Route)))];

    /// <summary>
    /// A broken unit that may rout and what it owes, such as "r1 (russian): must rout: ...; has routed", with a way to each place it may end; for a broken
    /// Passenger that has not routed, the vehicle it may rout beneath (D6.1; pass 65).
    /// </summary>
    public sealed record Obligation(string Unit, string Text, IReadOnlyList<Way>? Routes = null, string? Beneath = null);

    /// <summary>A broken Passenger routs beneath its vehicle (D6.1; pass 65, ruling R65.11).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnBeneath { get; set; }

    /// <summary>One least-cost route to a place a rout may end (pass 31d, design D3): the place, and the route as its Locations in order.</summary>
    public sealed record Way(string Target, string Route);

    /// <summary>What the chosen unit leaves and keeps before it routs (A10.4); null or empty for a unit that carries no more than its IPC.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Load { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The loads the unit may keep, when it has a choice among loads of equal PP.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Loads { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Keep { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnKeep { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<(string Unit, string Route)> OnUseRoute { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<Obligation> Obligations { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The broken units that may still rout this RtPh.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Units { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Unit { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public string Route { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public bool LowCrawl { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnUnit { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnRoute { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<bool> OnLowCrawl { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnPropose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the rout's lists and form are offered: not to the DEFENDER while the ATTACKER's routs come first (A10.5).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool RoutsOffered { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>The units of the view's side that may break voluntarily now (A10.41; pass 70, ruling R70.11).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<UnitSelectionList.Row> BreakRows { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlySet<string> BreakSelected { get; set; } = new HashSet<string>();

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<UnitSelectionList.Toggle> OnBreakToggle { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnProposeBreak { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The leaders who may rout with the chosen unit by Voluntary Rout (A10.711; pass 70, ruling R70.12).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Leaders { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Leader { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnLeader { get; set; }
}
